"prose": [
{
"from": 254,
"to": 265,
"text": "**The gates:** - a probe that no manifest or lock changed, measured from the base `b0e2d1c31`, HEAD when P4 wrote it; - the `--locked` workspace build; - the two crates' unit tests; - the new target; - the two edited virtual-node targets; - the stand companions that read the graph, actions, coverage, layout, exploration, masks, replay, spans, MCP, the   cross-OS digests and the canvas; - the seven_guis process checks that read the help and refusal texts and the hosts' logs; - the `a11y` leg, which runs `virtual_nodes_as_elements`; - the pre-push gate (`fast`), which runs the CI-script tests; - the `doc` leg, because the chunk edits public doc comments."
},
{
"from": 267,
"to": 274,
"text": "**What is absent:** - There is no boot-path touchpoint (no binary's start changes), so no smoke entry. - There is no live leg, and no headful self-verify harness in this project. - There is no `audit` leg: the probe holds every manifest and the lock unchanged. - There is no `stand-repeat`. The new target is no `stand_` file and joins no leg, so neither leg's pinned count   moves. - The coverage leg is not run locally. CI's coverage job reads the dioxus-native-dom (83 %) and escher-driver (97 %)   floors on the pushed tree, and the CI read asserts green over it."
},
{
"from": 276,
"to": 277,
"text": "**The controls** are step 14's one-shot runs. The diff adds two OS-conditional sites, step 9's `#[cfg(unix)]` cases, which the CI read names."
}
],
